From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] prntvpt: a printer's PrintCapabilities are its driver's papers, bins, duplex and more

PTGetPrintCapabilities wrote every feature empty. A program that chooses
its page from the capabilities found no paper: DYMO Connect looks for its
label among the PageMediaSize options and, finding none, asked for a
"custom" page of the label's printable area, which the printer's driver
did not have -- the label was laid out on another page and came out cut
off or shrunk. WPF's PrintDialog (System.Printing) had no sizes, trays or
duplex to offer.

The capabilities are now made from what the printer's driver tells
DeviceCapabilities, for any driver (a CUPS printer's PPD through wineps, a
printer maker's Windows driver through its DrvDeviceCapabilities): every
paper with its name and size (the print schema's names for Letter, A4...,
the driver's own papers as options of ours, "ns0000:Paper<number>"), a
custom size's range, the imageable area for the ticket's settings,
colour, resolutions, orientations, collation, duplex, the input bins
(psk:Manual, psk:Cassette... and the driver's own) and copies. A ticket
naming one of our paper options prints on that paper; a custom size the
driver has a paper of (within half a millimetre, either way round) is
that paper. Tickets carry the input bin and duplex both ways, the ticket
PTGetPrintCapabilities is given is optional and starts from the printer's
settings (a bin of -907431152 was written from uninitialised memory), and
a driver whose list of sizes leaves out its custom size is read right.

Test: test/ptcaps-gate.sh with test/ptcaps-probe.c, a CUPS server of its
own (mutants SG_MUTANT_PTCAPS, SG_MUTANT_PTPAPERNAME).
